@TITLE Theseus and the Minotaur
@AUTHOR Greek Myth (Public Domain)
@START athens_throne
@DESC_TEXT Slay the Minotaur in the labyrinth of Crete.

@ROOM athens_throne
@DESC
The throne room of Athens.
King Aegeus grips his chair,
face drawn with grief. Every
nine years, seven youths must
sail to Crete as tribute to
the dreaded Minotaur.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Volunteer to go" -> harbor
@CHOICE "Refuse the quest" -> refuse_quest

@ROOM refuse_quest
@DESC
Aegeus stares at you, broken.
Without a champion, the seven
youths are chosen by lot and
sent to their doom. Athens
weeps, and so do you.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "A hero must answer the call. Try again, Theseus."

@ROOM harbor
@DESC
The harbor of Athens. A black-
sailed ship rocks at anchor.
Sailors load provisions for
the grim voyage to Crete.
Aegeus clasps your shoulders.
"Return alive, my son."
@ENDDESC
@ITEM provisions "Provisions" "Salted meat, bread, and a skin of wine."
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Board the ship" -> ship_voyage

@ROOM ship_voyage
@DESC
The wine-dark sea stretches
to the horizon. Dolphins race
your bow. Crete is two days
hence. You have time to
prepare yourself.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Pray to Athena" -> ship_prayer
@CHOICE "Sharpen your blade" -> ship_blade
@CHOICE "Rest below decks" -> crete_arrival

@ROOM ship_prayer
@DESC
You kneel at the prow and
whisper to grey-eyed Athena.
The wind shifts, filling your
sails. A white owl circles
the mast, then vanishes.
You feel her favor upon you.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET athena_blessing
@CHOICE "Continue sailing" -> crete_arrival

@ROOM ship_blade
@DESC
You draw your iron blade and
work the whetstone until the
edge gleams like moonlight.
The other youths watch in
silence, hope kindling in
their eyes.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET sword_honed
@CHOICE "Continue sailing" -> crete_arrival

@ROOM crete_arrival
@DESC
The harbor of Knossos. White
stone walls blaze in the sun.
Bronze-armored guards line
the dock. They bind your
wrists and march you toward
the great palace.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Walk with dignity" -> palace_hall

@ROOM palace_hall
@DESC
The throne room of Knossos.
King Minos sits crowned in
gold, eyes cold as the sea.
"More Athenian lambs for the
beast," he sneers. A young
woman watches from the shadow.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Defy Minos boldly" -> palace_defiance
@CHOICE "Stay silent" -> palace_garden

@ROOM palace_defiance
@DESC
"I am Theseus, son of Aegeus.
I will slay your monster and
free Athens from this curse!"
Minos laughs, but the woman
in the shadows leans forward,
her dark eyes shining.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET minos_defied
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Go with the guards" -> palace_garden

@ROOM palace_garden
@DESC
Night. The palace garden is
silver with moonlight. Orange
trees scent the air. Tomorrow
you enter the labyrinth.
@IF minos_defied
A whisper from the colonnade:
"Theseus! Come quickly!"
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Speak with Ariadne" -> ariadne_meeting
@CHOICE "Sleep and rest" -> labyrinth_entrance

@ROOM ariadne_meeting
@DESC
Ariadne, daughter of Minos,
presses close. "I watched you
defy my father. Take these."
She gives you a bronze sword
and a ball of golden thread.
"Tie it at the entrance. It
will lead you back to me."
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET ariadne_ally
@ON_ENTER @SET has_thread
@ON_ENTER @SET has_sword
@ON_ENTER @GIVE thread
@ON_ENTER @GIVE bronze_sword
@SCORE +15
@CHOICE "Swear to return" -> labyrinth_entrance

@ROOM labyrinth_entrance
@DESC
Dawn. The great bronze doors
of the labyrinth yawn open.
Darkness breathes from within
like the mouth of a beast.
@IF has_thread
You tie the golden thread to
the door frame and step inside.
@ENDIF
@IF !has_thread
You step inside with nothing
but your courage and your fists.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go left" -> lab_bones
@CHOICE "Go right" -> lab_fountain
@CHOICE "Go straight" -> lab_dead_end

@ROOM lab_bones
@DESC
A corridor of cracked stone.
Bones litter the floor, the
remains of past tributes. A
skeleton clutches a battered
bronze shield.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM shield "Bronze Shield" "A dented but sturdy Athenian shield."
@CHOICE "Continue deeper" -> lab_chasm
@CHOICE "Turn back" -> labyrinth_entrance

@ROOM lab_fountain
@DESC
An underground spring trickles
from a crack in the wall into
a shallow basin. The water is
cold and sweet. A dark passage
leads further in.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM water_skin "Water Skin" "A leather skin filled with cool spring water."
@CHOICE "Follow the water" -> lab_dark_turn
@CHOICE "Turn back" -> labyrinth_entrance

@ROOM lab_dead_end
@DESC
The corridor narrows and ends
abruptly. Deep scratch marks
score the walls, as if some
beast clawed here in fury.
A faint draft stirs your hair.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go back" -> labyrinth_entrance

@ROOM lab_dark_turn
@DESC
The passage twists downward
into deeper darkness. You hear
water dripping somewhere far
below. The air grows warm
and stale.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Follow the passage" -> lab_offerings
@CHOICE "Go toward growling" -> lab_chasm
@CHOICE "Turn back" -> lab_fountain

@ROOM lab_offerings
@DESC
A low chamber lit by a crack
in the ceiling. Crumbled clay
offerings line the walls. Among
the rubble, something gleams:
a golden bull's horn, an
ancient votive treasure.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM golden_horn "Golden Horn" "A golden bull's horn, heavy and ancient."
@CHOICE "Go deeper" -> lab_chasm

@ROOM lab_chasm
@DESC
A vast chasm splits the maze.
Far below, black water churns.
A narrow stone bridge, barely
a foot wide, spans the gap.
The growling is louder here,
echoing from the depths.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Cross the bridge" -> lab_deep
@CHOICE "Jump the chasm" -> chasm_death
@CHOICE "Follow thread back" -> labyrinth_entrance @NEED has_thread

@ROOM chasm_death
@DESC
You leap, but the chasm is
too wide. You fall, spinning
into darkness. The black water
swallows you without a sound.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "The chasm claimed you. The bridge was the only way."

@ROOM lab_deep
@DESC
Deep in the labyrinth now.
The air is hot and rank with
the smell of beast. A low
rumbling growl vibrates through
the stone beneath your feet.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Follow the growling" -> lab_approach
@CHOICE "Retreat to the chasm" -> lab_chasm @NEED has_thread
@CHOICE "Turn away" -> lab_lost

@ROOM lab_lost
@DESC
You stumble through twisting
corridors. Every passage looks
the same. The walls close in.
The darkness is absolute.
@IF has_thread
A glint of gold -- the thread!
You seize it desperately.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Follow the thread" -> lab_deep @NEED has_thread
@CHOICE "Wander in darkness" -> lost_death @NEED !has_thread

@ROOM lost_death
@DESC
Hours pass. Days, perhaps.
You stumble on, throat burning
with thirst, until at last
your legs give way. The maze
has claimed another soul.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "You wandered until thirst took you. Ariadne's thread would have saved you."

@ROOM lab_approach
@DESC
The growling shakes loose dust
from the ceiling. A vast
archway opens before you,
carved with bulls and axes.
Beyond it, something enormous
breathes in the darkness.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Enter the chamber" -> minotaur_chamber

@ROOM minotaur_chamber
@DESC
The Minotaur. Half man, half
bull, huge as a galley. Its
horns scrape the ceiling. Red
eyes fix on you. It lowers
its head and charges with a
bellow that shakes the earth.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Attack with sword" -> minotaur_fight @NEED has_sword
@CHOICE "Brace with shield" -> minotaur_shield @NEED shield
@CHOICE "Try to reason" -> reason_death
@CHOICE "Flee" -> lab_lost

@ROOM reason_death
@DESC
You raise your hands and call
out to the beast. It does not
understand. It does not care.
The horns find you before your
words find meaning.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "The Minotaur knows no mercy. You needed a weapon."

@ROOM minotaur_fight
@DESC
You sidestep the charge and
drive Ariadne's bronze sword
deep between the beast's ribs.
It screams, a sound of ages.
It falls. The labyrinth shudders.
The Minotaur is slain.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET minotaur_slain
@SCORE +30
@CHOICE "Stand victorious" -> minotaur_dead

@ROOM minotaur_shield
@DESC
You plant your feet and raise
the shield. The beast's horns
slam into bronze. You hold.
It staggers. You strike with
a shard of broken horn. Again.
Again. At last it falls.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET minotaur_slain
@SCORE +25
@CHOICE "Stand victorious" -> minotaur_dead

@ROOM minotaur_dead
@DESC
The beast lies still. Blood
pools on ancient stone. Silence
fills the labyrinth for the
first time in a thousand years.
You must find your way out.
@IF has_thread
The golden thread gleams at
your feet, leading home.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@CHOICE "Follow the thread" -> labyrinth_exit @NEED has_thread
@CHOICE "Search for an exit" -> escape_hard @NEED !has_thread

@ROOM escape_hard
@DESC
You stumble through corridors
for hours, bleeding and lost.
At last, a sliver of daylight.
You claw through rubble into
blinding sun, half-dead but
free. No one waits for you.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Stagger to the ship" -> escape_crete

@ROOM labyrinth_exit
@DESC
You follow the golden thread
through every twist and turn,
back across the chasm bridge,
past the bones and the spring,
to the great bronze doors.
Sunlight floods your eyes.
@IF ariadne_ally
Ariadne rushes to embrace you,
tears streaming down her face.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@CHOICE "Run to the ship" -> escape_crete

@ROOM escape_crete
@DESC
You race through the sleeping
city to the harbor. The other
Athenian youths are already
aboard. You cast off the lines
and the black-sailed ship
surges into open water.
@IF ariadne_ally
Ariadne stands at the prow,
her hand in yours.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Set course for Athens" -> return_voyage

@ROOM return_voyage
@DESC
The sea is calm. Athens rises
on the horizon. You remember
your father's last words: "If
you live, change the black
sails to white, so I will
know from the cliffs."
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Change to white sails" -> victory_white
@CHOICE "Forget the sails" -> victory_tragic

@ROOM victory_white
@DESC
You raise the white sails.
They catch the wind and blaze
like wings against the blue
sky. On the cliffs of Athens,
old Aegeus sees them and falls
to his knees, weeping with joy.
All Athens celebrates the hero
who ended the Minotaur's reign.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +50
@WIN "Theseus triumphs! White sails bring joy. Score: {score}"

@ROOM victory_tragic
@DESC
In your weariness and triumph,
you forget your father's plea.
The black sails billow as you
approach Athens. On the cliffs,
Aegeus sees them and believes
you dead. Mad with grief, the
old king hurls himself into
the sea that will bear his name.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +30
@WIN "You slew the beast, but forgot the sails. The Aegean Sea is named for your father's sorrow. Score: {score}"
